      "quoted": {
        "id": "2091270624811335794",
        "text": "No amount of penance will suffice to stop the suicide of the West. \n\nIn 2006, Pascal Bruckner diagnosed the illness as “Western masochism”, a civilization so convinced its own sins explain every problem on earth that it turns self-hatred into a strange form of narcissism.\n\n>Corporate America pledged over $50 billion in racial equity penance after George Floyd\n>California set up a slavery reparations task force even though it entered the Union in 1850 as a free state that never legalized slavery\n>The New York Times pushed the 1619 Project claiming slavery was the real founding, then edited the most absurd claims instead of retracting them\n\nA nation that can only feel guilty eventually loses the capacity to feel proud of anything, and a people that cannot defend their own story will not keep one for long.",
